# Units that open /etc/substrate/private or /workspace/.substrate-private AT RUNTIME and therefore override the
# default-deny drop-in service.d/05-secret-dir-out-of-reach.conf with a same-named
# file in their own <unit>.service.d/. One list; nothing implicit. (systemd reads only
# *.conf in a drop-in directory, so this file configures nothing.)
# Read by validation/scripts/secret-dir-mask.test.sh: every entry has its override,
# every override has its entry. A unit that only LOADS a secret (EnvironmentFile=)
# needs no exemption and must not have one.
# Format: <unit> <reason>
identity-seeder.service      seed-identity writes the minted SUBSTRATE_ADMIN_KEY / METABOB_API_KEY into private/admin.env, its consumers' private/env.d files and the persisted store
substrate-pull-sync.service  renders, migrates and retires the scoped files and the store (render-secret-scope), vessel-ctl install merges into both (secrets.env.sh), and runs secret-mask-probe check, which must stat the real files
git-push-setup.service       setup-git-push sources the persisted store for the push credential (SUBSTRATE_GIT_PAT)
